NMSF Dataset: Multimodal Depression Diagnosis

The NMSF (Neuro-Speech Functional) dataset is designed for research in multimodal depression diagnosis, providing a comprehensive set of speech and resting-state fMRI data. This dataset includes samples of individuals with Major Depression (MD) and Healthy Controls (HC), along with demographic information.

Dataset Details:

Speech Data: All speech signals are resampled at 16 kHz and saved in .WAV format.

fMRI Data: The resting-state fMRI data are acquired with the following parameters:

Repetition Time (TR): 500 ms

Echo Time (TE): 30 ms

Field of View (FOV): 224 × 224 mm²

Voxel Size: 3.5 × 3.5 × 3.5 mm³

Slice Spacing: 0 mm

35 slices per volume

960 time points

Preprocessing was conducted using the SPM12 and DPARSF toolbox with the following steps:

Removal of the first 10 volumes

Slice timing correction

Head motion correction

Spatial normalization to MNI standard space (3 × 3 × 3 mm³ voxels)

Spatial smoothing with a 6 mm FWHM Gaussian kernel

Temporal bandpass filter (0.01–0.08 Hz)

The brain is parcellated into 90 regions of interest (ROIs) based on the Automated Anatomical Labeling (AAL) atlas. The mean signal of all voxels within each ROI is extracted for further analysis.

Demographic Information:

Age range: 19-39 years

Groups: Healthy Controls (HC) and Major Depression (MD)

Gender: 53 male and 150 female participants

For more details on data acquisition and preprocessing, please refer to the full documentation.
